069425 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43bca481-7d34-5259-91cb-874aca82b8b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498885} {:answer/id #uuid "4f0d4325-0f8d-5187-a9a0-6346e4c4c09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3(x-1)^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498914} {:answer/id #uuid "6831cc29-926d-5a0f-9b44-864c4b8510e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3(1-x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498964} {:answer/id #uuid "75522216-0f2f-585a-a400-b83699659bdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "27(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498991} {:answer/id #uuid "8516910a-3ad3-5900-bf26-9abcee760676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3(x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499029}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499029} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c8712f6-aae6-50a7-bb10-c5dc0c11f25f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067720}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "49c6fb96-74c6-5438-982d-666dbe67b2e9" :question/math-academy-id "q-52493" :question/problem "Simplify $\\sqrt[3]{27(x-1)^{3}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the expression, we write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{27(x-1)^{3}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{3(x-1)\\cdot 3(x-1)\\cdot 3(x-1)} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(3(x-1))}^{3}} & = \\\\ 3(x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "b51e797c-a377-52f5-acf1-019291d3535d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499576}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499629 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186499461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34df0886-f589-5a77-91fd-b574dff15d23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{a}{4{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498850} {:answer/id #uuid "4869d8e8-8306-5d02-89de-d7b839a472df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{a}{2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498896} {:answer/id #uuid "669efc65-a593-55a2-9cb2-e9832fd6adb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{a}{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498959} {:answer/id #uuid "9d702685-480a-51e1-930a-6e01b50056fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a}{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499064} {:answer/id #uuid "b0037796-de78-55f7-b178-e17d9506d50d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{a}{8x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499117}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186498896} :answer-field/id #uuid "efd8c6c1-d268-5074-8c20-054b800150f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499424}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3ee83331-c90f-5e77-b2f4-e2b981936cc1" :question/math-academy-id "q-82157" :question/problem "Find $\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{{a}^{3}}{8{x}^{3}}}.$" :question/worked-solution "To simplify the expression, we write the term under the radical as a perfect cube, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{-\\frac{{a}^{3}}{8{x}^{3}}} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{(-\\frac{a}{2x})\\cdot (-\\frac{a}{2x})\\cdot (-\\frac{a}{2x})} & = \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{{(-\\frac{a}{2x})}^{3}} & = \\\\ -\\frac{a}{2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e5848270-698c-55c8-973b-062f99103d08"}] :activity/title "The Cube Root of a Perfect Cube With Algebraic Expressions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186498726}] [{:activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069617} :activity/id #uuid "10771a71-8e46-50cc-b75f-ab2b84a9afeb" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187 :topic/id #uuid "86a29d40-d28e-53d5-b56d-cdcc72f7fe80" :topic/math-academy-id 430} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069617 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070019 :tutorial/content "When an equation contains an $x^2$ term and a constant, it can be solved using the **square root method**. The square root method makes use of the fact that\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x^2} = \\vert x \\vert \\,.\n$$\n\nTo illustrate, we can solve the equation $2x^2-18=0$ using the following three steps:\n\n1\\. Isolate the $x^2$ on one side of the equation:\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-18 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2} & =18 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =9\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n2\\. Take the square root of both sides of the equation\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\ |x| & =3\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\n3\\. Solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n  $$\n  \\begin{aligned}x & =3\\,\\text{or}\\,x=-3\\end{aligned}\n  $$\n\nSo, there are two solutions, $x=3$ and $x=-3.$ We can write this more concisely as $x= \\pm 3,$ where the \"$\\pm$\" symbol stands for \"plus or minus.\"" :tutorial/id #uuid "7ef92091-e041-5715-ac4e-75fa146c4cea" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8692 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "6a92a024-3077-5b06-9926-573d76e002f6" :step/math-academy-id 165690 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069618}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069618 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068725 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068475 :question/id #uuid "fed35802-1128-5cb4-a91b-e98227dcfba8" :question/math-academy-id "e-13966"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f544d0a4-24ce-5078-ad9d-93e733c091e6" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048267} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049843}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069222} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069263} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069340} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487308} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487400}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations With Integer Solutions"} :step/id #uuid "e261bc60-5f18-5ce3-8444-d66fb71d6b56" :step/math-academy-id 165691 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069619}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069619 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068726 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068476 :question/id #uuid "6145c2d5-5d09-543c-8405-1319277323aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-13968"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6c5d24fa-8a65-5c20-bb50-530ca8dcf061" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050315}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069138} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069173} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069341} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487300} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487346} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492907} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492916} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545849}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations With Fractional Solutions"} :step/id #uuid "f81f6359-676f-52fc-9e50-90a17ad8c71b" :step/math-academy-id 165695 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069620}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069620 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068727 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068477 :question/id #uuid "9c00e3e1-9337-5380-af51-e7e8c7ae9f48" :question/math-academy-id "e-13970"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a21c64f2-1b4b-54b3-a8a1-70ca63330e04" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049923}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069036} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069139} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069163} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487289} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487296} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487318} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186487406} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492883} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545817} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545838}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations With Radical Solutions"} :step/id #uuid "116d4e70-b784-54f1-b8a9-1880b475e2a2" :step/math-academy-id 165699}] :activity/title "Solving Equations Using the Square Root Method" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186068962}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046648} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492934} :activity/id #uuid "e5862109-bc69-574a-aa55-2c8e894e10bd" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187 :topic/id #uuid "86a29d40-d28e-53d5-b56d-cdcc72f7fe80" :topic/math-academy-id 430} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492934 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492907 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a6f09a0-ccd7-5f3c-b936-37c4d8190186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492363} {:answer/id #uuid "72c93668-102e-59cf-bbee-5a2ec27c8f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{3}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492444} {:answer/id #uuid "8bbf1f51-b87d-56f3-a2e4-c8c1a5907fb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492494} {:answer/id #uuid "aabe0e05-f4e4-5dba-8d77-0379c8bb7619" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{3}{49}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492562} {:answer/id #uuid "d05fdd44-d514-56b7-a034-70edb6be2559" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "x=\\pm \\frac{9}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492631}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492444} :answer-field/id #uuid "52cb84e8-9f4d-596d-8658-8754ec0aa693" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c009e53d-f124-53fe-9bd5-4569b0faacf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-78906" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}=\\frac{9}{98}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${x}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2} & =\\frac{9}{98} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{9\\cdot 2}{98} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =\\frac{9}{49}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{49}} \\\\ |x| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{9}}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\ |x| & =\\frac{3}{7} \\\\ x & =\\pm \\frac{3}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "1c1afa0a-f568-5caf-ba70-ff3df6c7dca6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492940}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492940 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7524c348-11f2-59fe-89ce-2554d91064a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pm \\frac{5}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492451}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492451} :answer-field/id #uuid "246155e5-4b6f-5296-89cb-0ce66033efc4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492717}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dc9b5d6a-36da-5369-a8e0-149a58110d0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-218577" :question/problem "If $49{a}^{2}+12=37,$ then $a=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${a}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}49{a}^{2}+12 & =37 \\\\ 49{a}^{2} & =25 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{49}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{49}} \\\\ |a| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\ |a| & =\\frac{5}{7} \\\\ a & =\\pm \\frac{5}{7}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3342109e-04c1-5840-b62d-667fd5a7fffe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492966}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492966 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492883 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b1bc9b8-0ea0-52cc-a644-25016e73c24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pm 3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492465}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492465} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb6954e1-945b-51aa-b2d8-20a643556b8d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492816}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "90d6c1a2-df8a-556c-89a1-d672dd78eab8" :question/math-academy-id "q-218588" :question/problem "Solve the equation ${v}^{2}=45.$ Express your final answer in its simplest form.\n\n$v=$\n\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{v}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\ |v| & =\\sqrt{9\\cdot 5} \\\\ |v| & =\\sqrt{9}\\cdot \\sqrt{5} \\\\ |v| & =3\\sqrt{5} \\\\ v & =\\pm 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "88a5c700-3e29-5300-852c-85cc903204b4"}] :activity/title "Solving Equations Using the Square Root Method" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186492220}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046647} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545914} :activity/id #uuid "baea3878-87f7-5c2d-97d8-1054599f9f7d" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048187 :topic/id #uuid "86a29d40-d28e-53d5-b56d-cdcc72f7fe80" :topic/math-academy-id 430} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545914 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000f3d81-c5d0-5946-b172-3bf3fe65444a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=\\pm 2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545200} {:answer/id #uuid "34ac2f0d-2f64-5eae-b276-d1d7570929cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=-2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545305} {:answer/id #uuid "43f62726-6db5-59d8-a65d-6482ea48a157" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545328} {:answer/id #uuid "492c1b78-ce03-55b1-9771-7be25a941eaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=\\pm 2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545338} {:answer/id #uuid "9ba5b039-42c1-5f88-a8de-65c4f49d3c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "a=2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545481}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545200} :answer-field/id #uuid "74304a95-1479-50c8-b9fd-11f3f0128771" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "9a2ec726-00b7-5cc7-85a6-cb62e4711dd2" :question/math-academy-id "q-12796" :question/problem "Find $a$ if ${a}^{2}=40.$" :question/worked-solution "We take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 10} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{10} \\\\ |a| & =2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ a & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "3f35f28c-8140-5525-adb9-84b98af741a1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545958}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545953 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545849 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "363dd3dd-0402-51c3-b564-d0f77502fd2e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\pm 5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545311} {:answer/id #uuid "58910719-15f1-5c10-aba5-c08657d568a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\pm 6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545366} {:answer/id #uuid "5d867956-1afa-545a-8d5e-158bee736d9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\pm \\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545377} {:answer/id #uuid "9ee5e500-cf1f-5e17-88ce-c0068943b54e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\pm \\frac{6}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545492} {:answer/id #uuid "dae9e2a6-948b-5b95-a02c-61c1a8d0f2ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "z=\\frac{5}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545605}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545377} :answer-field/id #uuid "2138cdc1-7319-514a-94f4-c743a1b5525e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545687}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "af7384d0-ffc3-51cc-833d-b329ee1b978c" :question/math-academy-id "q-111429" :question/problem "Solve for $z$ where $3{z}^{2}-\\frac{25}{12}=0.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${z}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}^{2}-\\frac{25}{12} & =0 \\\\ 3{z}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{12} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\frac{25}{36}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{z}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{25}{36}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{\\sqrt{25}}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\ |z| & =\\frac{5}{6} \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{5}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "9976cbb6-bd4a-584c-b73f-c65c17b1a0de"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545958 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545817 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "174968af-4f97-5fc2-96c1-946a1318679f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pm 2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545243} {:answer/id #uuid "1787098a-f4be-583e-8b74-371cf41e0f4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pm 3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545244} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6a6925-66ac-5529-a6b8-a5006b6b8998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pm 4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545260} {:answer/id #uuid "260a6d7a-9e0e-525f-a529-7e99511654a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pm \\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545281} {:answer/id #uuid "81d4dc11-5639-5bc7-9888-4db8339d8ad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545440}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545440} :answer-field/id #uuid "825ca9e2-d349-54be-8ff8-677e119c487a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "48d8f1b2-776f-5613-8b52-d9e267acd25f" :question/math-academy-id "q-56116" :question/problem "Find $a$ if ${a}^{2}-6=6.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the ${a}^{2}$ on one side of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}^{2}-6 & =6 \\\\ {a}^{2} & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we take the square root of both sides of the equation and solve the resulting absolute value equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{{a}^{2}} & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{4\\cdot 3} \\\\ |a| & =\\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ |a| & =2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ a & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a00c9687-cbb9-5d05-9d5b-a0e30fddfa25" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186545953}}] :activity/title "Solving Equations Using the Square Root Method" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186545193}] [{:activity/expected-seconds 660.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069592} :activity/id #uuid "a94cc1b0-429b-5583-ab2e-ced406c12a6a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048267 :topic/id #uuid "8dee6cdf-6bc7-52db-8873-a393c17a11e1" :topic/math-academy-id 384} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070024 :tutorial/content "In this lesson, we'll learn how to solve equations that contain absolute value expressions.\n\nFor example, let's consider the following equation:\n\n$$\n|x+1| = 4\n$$\n\nFor this equation to be true, either the *positive or negative* of the expression inside the absolute value must equal the right-hand side. That is,\n\n$$\nx+1 = 4 \\qquad\\qquad \\text{ or } \\qquad\\qquad -(x+1)=4.\n$$\n\nSo, let's solve these two equations:\n\n- First, we solve the equation $x+1 = 4{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & =4 \\\\ x+1-1 & =4-1 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Then, we solve the equation $-(x+1) = 4{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(x+1) & =4 \\\\ -x-1 & =4 \\\\ -x-1+1 & =4+1 \\\\ -x & =5 \\\\ x & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original absolute value equation are $x={\\color{blue}3}$ and $x={\\color{red}{-5}}.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "35d16431-4611-59fc-8888-c1db1a7b9902" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8821 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "0212403d-0f66-5be5-8ebb-0dcacbe7f08f" :step/math-academy-id 143132 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069593}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186070025 :tutorial/content "So, we've seen that the solutions to the equation \n\n$$\n|x+1| = 4\n$$\n\nare $x={\\color{blue}3}$ and $x={\\color{red}{-5}}.$ \n\nWe can verify that these solutions are correct by substituting them back into the original equation and checking we get a true statement:\n\n- Substituting $x={\\color{blue}3}$ into our equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+1| & =4 \\\\ |3+1| & =4 \\\\ |4| & =4 \\\\ 4 & =4.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x={\\color{blue}3}$ is indeed a solution to the absolute value equation.\n\n- Substituting $x={\\color{red}-5}$ into our equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|x+1| & =4 \\\\ |-5+1| & =4 \\\\ |-4| & =4 \\\\ 4 & =4.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x={\\color{red}-5}$ is indeed a solution to the absolute value equation.\n\nTherefore, $x={\\color{blue}3}$ and $x={\\color{red}{-5}}$ are both solutions to our absolute value equation." :tutorial/id #uuid "561ffe88-9340-5e0a-840a-6946f446a9f2" :tutorial/math-academy-id 8822 :tutorial/title "Checking the Solution"} :step/id #uuid "88ed50f9-5a31-59c8-9fca-2e1513db0b7a" :step/math-academy-id 143133 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069594}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17